{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.VolumeTranscendental","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.VolumeTranscendental","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Algebraic.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Algebraic.Basic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.volTranscendental_imp_irrational","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.volTranscendental_imp_irrational","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/VolumeTranscendental.lean#L109-L113","doc":"**The transcendence rung sits strictly between the two the file already\ndraws**: it implies irrationality of `vol_4_1`, and is not implied by it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.volTranscendental","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.volTranscendental","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/VolumeTranscendental.lean#L67-L107","doc":"**`Vol(4₁)` is transcendental over ℚ**, conditional on algebraic independence.\n\nRestricting `HyperbolicVolumeIndependence.no_relation` to the `(i, 0, 0)`\nslice — where `vol_5_2 ^ 0 = vol_B3 ^ 0 = 1` — says that no nonzero rational\npolynomial annihilates `vol_4_1`, which is transcendence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.slice_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.slice_injective","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/VolumeTranscendental.lean#L62-L65","doc":"The slice map `i ↦ (i, 0, 0)` is injective. ","signatureChunk":0}]}